When conducting a systematic literature review (SLR), there are several important steps.

We need to search for relevant studies, select the studies, extract data, assess their quality, and synthesise the findings.

One important step is certainty assessment.

Certainty assessment helps us understand how confident we can be in the evidence from the included studies.

